# Machine-checked equivalence proof for the IGLA RACE ternary MAC.
#
# Theorem T1: for ALL 8-bit signed activations a, ALL 2-bit weight codes
# w_code, and ALL 32-bit signed accumulator inputs acc_in, the shipped
# multiplier-free RTL (ternary_mac_top) produces exactly the same acc_out as
# a golden model that uses a real `*` operator (ternary_mac_golden).
#
# Method: build a sequential miter over the two designs and ask the SAT solver
# to find ANY input assignment, over one clocked transition, where the outputs
# differ.  "SAT proof finished - no model found" == no such assignment exists.
#
# Run: yosys -s prove_ternary_mac.ys

read_verilog ../verilog/ternary_mac_synth.v
read_verilog ternary_mac_golden.v

prep

miter -equiv -flatten -make_assert ternary_mac_top ternary_mac_golden miter_mac
hierarchy -top miter_mac
prep -top miter_mac
async2sync

# -tempinduct, not -seq N.  This design is sound under a bounded check only
# because `acc_in` is an input PORT with no path from `acc_out` back into the
# logic, so one enabled frame is already exhaustive -- a structural property
# nothing in the flow verifies.  Close that loop in a refactor and a bounded
# check keeps printing SUCCESS while proving strictly less than the theorem
# above claims.  Temporal induction quantifies over ALL reachable states and
# discharges in 0.27 s.  See T115 in docs/theory/IGLA-FORMAL-RESULTS.md.
sat -verify -prove-asserts -tempinduct -set-init-zero -show-inputs -show-outputs miter_mac
